the first trailer for the Twilight Zone  2019 remake has just dropped and whilst  there flies by in less than 90 seconds  there's still a lot to unpack from it  The Twilight Zone is a show that I  absolutely adored growing up and in my  college years I spent hours upon hours  watching the episodes my favorite ever  one was called the howling man and it's  centered around a man stumbling across a  secret cult during a storm that believed  they managed to capture the devil and  lock him up as a prisoner the man  eventually discovers him and he sees  he's just a frail polite young man and  during the episode he tries to convince  him to say I'm free I don't want to  spoil the ending but it has an  incredible twist and whilst that episode  itself doesn't appear to be getting  remade there are actually three in the  trailer that appear to be from the  original series throughout this video  I'll be breaking down everything that  you need to know about those episodes as  well as giving my thoughts on the series  as a whole there will be heavy spoilers  here so if you don't want to know  anything in regards to the show then I  highly suggest that you turn off now for  everyone else don't adjust your YouTube  channel just sit back relax and enjoy my  breakdown of the twilight zone trailer  okay the first major episode that we can  definitely confirm is a remake of  Nightmare at 20,000 feet this classic  episode followed William Shatner on a  plane as he was slowly driven insane by  a monster that appeared to be destroying  the fuselage from the outside Shatner is  the only one that can apparently see it  and the episode centers around him  trying to convince the other passengers  that he's not crazy the episode has been  parodied by Ace Ventura The Simpsons and  even Johnny Bravo it's definitely the  show signature episode and even got  remade in the Twilight Zone film in 1983  the floating head that we see at the  beginning of the new trailer is the same  as the monsters and it definitely  appears that the episode we'll follow is  similar tale where it differs is that we  see the main protagonists off the plane  and by a lake it appears that his  journey will continue beyond the plane  as in the original  episode it was restricted to this the  episode ended with Shatner being  escorted away but the camera lingered on  the plane's engine long enough to show  that it had been damaged  whether Jordan peeler will take this  route isn't clear but it's certainly an  interesting take the second episode that  appears to be a remake is the one where  it's clear that a child is running for  president whilst it's not a direct  adaptation this seems to be sticking  pretty closely to the episode titled  it's a good life in that a young boy  possesses incredible almost godlike  mental powers and he's able to read and  control Minds this pretty much puts  everyone at his mercy and all those who  offend him are killed in the episode the  boy named Anthony isolates his town from  the rest of the world and rules it as a  tyrant  however just being a young boy he has  absolutely no idea how to run industry  agriculture and so on thus the town  slowly starts to die and crumble in on  itself however everyone is so terrified  of Anthony that they pretend like  everything is going amazingly the acting  is fantastic and throughout all of the  adults kind of smile through gritted  teeth in its modern adaptation I can  imagine this being a very clear Trump  metaphor with the president being  portrayed as a spoiled brat which is  something that those opposite Trump  often call him it's definitely an  interesting take and is something that  cements just how necessary that the  twilight zone is in today's climate the  third episode is called in the nick of  time and this centers around the devil  head machine that we see in the trailer  in the original work this was a  fortune-telling device a couple begin to  test it and slowly realize that it's  very very accurate they eventually are  led to believe that it's unsafe to leave  the diner that they're occupying at 3:00  p.m. and one of the characters becomes  obsessed with this notion it's basically  about how there's no future but what we  make for ourselves and that worry will  forever hold us back  it's a neat one to remake as it's  definitely one of the more niche  episodes but I can't wait to see how it  plays out I can't wait to see what the  other episodes offer I would have liked  to a focus on them but I'm not too sure  exactly what plot route they will take  and it would have just purely been  speculation whereas these episodes I  feel they're definitely gonna go this  way  if you want to know more about those  episodes then make sure you stay tuned  to the channel for full breakdowns on  them upon their release on the CBS  streaming service on April 1st  obviously I'd love to hear your thoughts  on the trailer and if there's anything  that I missed comment below and let me  know and if you enjoy this video then  please like it and check out my  breakdown of the haunting of Bligh Manor  trailer which will be linked at the end  this is a channel for people who are  never missing television so if that's  the kind of thing you like you need to  subscribe to definition thanks again for  taking the time to watch this you've  been the best I'll see you next time  take care peace  [Music]  [Music]
 

